+# Epic Breakdown: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard  
+**Date**: 2026-08-10  
+**Total Epics**: 3 (E000 plus 2 product epics)  
+**Estimated Total Stories**: 13–22
+
+---
+
+## Epic Dependency Map
+
+```text
+E000 Developer Infrastructure → E001 Transcript Review Foundation → E002 Confirmed Reminder Delivery
+```
+
+## Epic Prioritization
+
+### MVP Epics
+
+- E000: Developer Infrastructure
+- E001: Workspace-Scoped Transcript Review
+- E002: Confirmed Reminder Delivery
+
+### Deferred Scope
+
+- Meeting recording, calendar replacement, and autonomous outbound messaging are explicitly out of scope.
+- Market expansion and new provider capabilities are not planned without new evidence.
+
+## Epic Definitions
+
+### E000: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Value Statement**: This epic gives the two-engineer pilot a repeatable way to test, validate, and operate the upload-to-confirmation-to-delivery path.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Establish local lint, test, and build commands; CI for those checks; environment/configuration conventions; and test support for the real request path. Configure operational visibility appropriate to the selected runtime, including a way to inspect reminder delivery failures. It does not choose the reminder provider or implement product workflows.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A developer can run lint, tests, and the browser/API build locally with documented commands.
+- [ ] CI runs the same relevant checks for proposed changes.
+- [ ] Environment configuration keeps provider credentials outside source control.
+- [ ] The project can exercise and capture evidence for the end-to-end pilot path, including real-request-role isolation probes.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- API and browser-UI project scaffolding with local quality commands
+- Test framework and fixture patterns for the pilot path
+- CI pipeline for lint, tests, and build
+- Environment configuration and operational error/delivery diagnostics
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: None
+- **Enables**: E001 and E002
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: —
+- Models/Services: Test and configuration support to be selected during epic specification
+- Files/Components: CI configuration, quality-tool configuration, environment templates, and test harnesses
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 4–6  
+**Priority**: P0 — Foundation  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 0
+
+### E001: Workspace-Scoped Transcript Review
+
+**Value Statement**: This epic enables meeting facilitators to upload a transcript and review workspace-scoped proposed action items, so meeting follow-up becomes visible without any autonomous scheduling.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Create the minimum workspace boundary, transcript intake, action-proposal extraction, and browser review surface. Extraction produces reviewable proposals only. The epic enforces that a workspace cannot read another workspace's transcripts or proposed actions, but it does not schedule or send reminders.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A facilitator can upload a transcript into their workspace and see proposed action items.
+- [ ] A facilitator can review and edit proposal text before it becomes a confirmed action.
+- [ ] No extraction or review action schedules a reminder.
+- [ ] A real-request-role negative probe demonstrates that another workspace cannot read the transcript or its action proposals.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Workspace context and request-path access boundary
+- Transcript upload and workspace-scoped persistence
+- Proposed-action extraction from an uploaded transcript
+- Browser review and editing of proposed actions
+- Cross-workspace isolation tests using the real request role
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000
+- **Enables**: E002
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: Workspace, transcript, and proposed-action persistence to be designed in epic planning
+- Models/Services: Python API request authorization, transcript ingestion, action-proposal extraction
+- Files/Components: Browser transcript-upload and action-review surfaces
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 5–8  
+**Priority**: P0 — MVP Critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 1
+
+### E002: Confirmed Reminder Delivery
+
+**Value Statement**: This epic enables facilitators to explicitly confirm an action's text, owner, and due date, then receive one provider-delivered reminder with visible status.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Add the server-enforced confirmation gate, reminder scheduling, a configurable provider boundary, and delivery-status display to reviewed actions from E001. Provider choice is intentionally deferred; the implementation must prove the selected provider in the real end-to-end path. It does not add calendar replacement or autonomous outbound behavior.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] Scheduling cannot occur until a facilitator explicitly confirms text, owner, and due date.
+- [ ] A confirmed action results in exactly one reminder through the configured provider.
+- [ ] The facilitator can inspect the reminder's delivery status.
+- [ ] Runtime evidence exercises upload, proposal review, explicit confirmation, delivery, and status inspection.
+- [ ] A facilitator LARP judges the complete path as usable and clear about the human confirmation boundary.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Confirmation UI and server-side state gate for text, owner, and due date
+- Reminder scheduling for confirmed actions
+- Configurable reminder-provider adapter and credentials handling
+- Delivery-status capture and browser presentation
+- End-to-end runtime test, real-request-role isolation probe, and facilitator LARP
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000, E001
+- **Enables**: Pilot measurement
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: Confirmed-action and reminder-delivery state, if persistence is required by the selected design
+- Models/Services: Python confirmation gate, reminder scheduler, provider adapter, delivery-status service
+- Files/Components: Browser confirmation, due-date/owner review, and delivery-status surfaces
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 4–8  
+**Priority**: P0 — MVP Critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 2
+
+## Epic Execution Strategy
+
+### Phase 0: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Goal**: make pilot development and proof repeatable before product workflows start.
+
+- E000 runs first and enables all following epics.
+- Success gate: local and CI quality paths work, configuration is safe, and test support exists for the evidence contract.
+
+### Phase 1: Transcript Review Foundation
+
+**Goal**: deliver the useful, safe proposal-review slice without sending reminders.
+
+- E001 begins after E000.
+- Success gate: facilitators can upload, view, and review workspace-scoped proposals; the real request path rejects cross-workspace reads.
+
+### Phase 2: Confirmed Reminder Delivery
+
+**Goal**: complete the human-confirmed follow-through path.
+
+- E002 begins after E001.
+- Success gate: the runtime path reaches delivery status only after explicit confirmation, and the facilitator LARP is performed at validation.
+
+## Risk Mitigation by Epic
+
+| Epic | Primary Risk | Mitigation Strategy |
+|------|--------------|-------------------|
+| E000 | Pilot work is not reproducible or observable | Establish repeatable local/CI checks and test/evidence harnesses first |
+| E001 | Cross-workspace access or unsafe extraction-to-send behavior | Enforce request-path isolation and keep proposals unscheduled until E002 confirmation |
+| E002 | Unselected provider or confirmation bypass | Isolate provider selection behind configuration; enforce and prove the confirmation gate server-side |
+
+## Success Metrics by Epic
+
+| Epic | Key Metric | Target | Measurement |
+|------|------------|--------|-------------|
+| E000 | Reproducible quality path | Relevant local and CI commands pass | CI and documented local commands |
+| E001 | Proposal review coverage | Inputs produce reviewable proposals; 80% review target tracked for pilot | Proposal and review events |
+| E002 | Accountable follow-through | One confirmed reminder exposes delivery status; 0 bypasses | Runtime path evidence and scheduling records |
+
+## Notes
+
+- This is a serial plan: E002 integrates directly with the action proposal and workspace boundary from E001. No concurrency-wave table is required for this three-epic Build plan.
+- Story estimates are planning ranges and will be refined during epic planning.
+- `/project-analyze` is recommended before the first `/epic-specify`; it is not the mandatory four-or-more-epic gate because this plan contains three epics total.
